{"id": "EUVD-2026-81698", "enisaUuid": "0d4731a7-1b7d-304d-acc5-1009ae0144d7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvxlan: fix reading neigh ha\n\nCurrently arp/neigh_reduce read neigh ha directly which can lead to\npartial reads while the neigh is being updated. Use neigh_ha_snapshot to\ntake a stable snapshot of the address similar to route_shortcircuit which\nalready does the right thing.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:49:52", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6093baf2b2c57e7da33bacd2223570a78b416d89", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/751cb520f9e47538b7223df133806a29fc41f54f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f43ef9a3f9c121472a0754c9e9bff13317ace0f7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ecc8bac11a101e5f6989a14b92e17b51f9761630", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b824059a673b2283e78c7aae2c7d257aad7f0e1d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6mp3-g7qw-8rgw", "CVE-2026-90105"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0bdd86bc-8cec-3c3a-8093-96bc9bf67442", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "0cbca3d8-96ad-35ee-8a02-cad828a1665f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e4f67addf158f98f8197e08974966b18480dc751 <b824059a673b2283e78c7aae2c7d257aad7f0e1d"}, {"id": "285a2277-4068-3ea6-882a-71921a69ef30", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "2a995df0-1cf6-38a1-a5fb-59dee9c3146b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e4f67addf158f98f8197e08974966b18480dc751 <751cb520f9e47538b7223df133806a29fc41f54f"}, {"id": "3b6aa768-4bb8-316c-9344-2f6810e9d58e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.8"}, {"id": "457a5740-90dc-336d-bf74-7de5d380d8bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "pr